---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// TODO(store): the "Buy a license" link points at "#" until the store URL
// exists. Point it at the Lemon Squeezy checkout (or the product page that
// leads to it) once it is live — the same destination the plugin's Buy button
// opens.
---

<Layout
  title="Radical Process"
  description="SGD (Spatial Gesture Designer) turns a sound file into a gesture that travels through a virtual room around the listener. Binaural VST3 / AU / Standalone plugin for macOS."
>

  <!-- ── HEADER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <header class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-14 pb-4">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
      <img src="/img/logo.png" alt="Radical Process" class="h-9 w-auto shrink-0" />
      <p class="text-xs uppercase text-gray-400">
        <span class="tracking-[0.45em] text-gray-200">Radical Process</span>
        <span class="text-gray-400 tracking-[0.25em]">
          &nbsp;—&nbsp; Unapologetically niche, unapologetically deep
        </span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ── SGD ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20">

    <section class="pt-10">
      <div class="mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-x-8 gap-y-5">
        <div>
          <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-black tracking-tighter mb-1">SGD</h1>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm tracking-wide uppercase">
            Spatial Gesture Designer &nbsp;·&nbsp; VST3 / AU / Standalone &nbsp;·&nbsp; macOS
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="#download"
             class="inline-block border border-gray-500 hover:border-gray-300 px-6 py-4 text-gray-200 hover:text-white transition-colors text-sm tracking-[0.25em] uppercase">
            Download
          </a>
          <a href="#"
             class="inline-block border border-gray-500 hover:border-gray-300 px-6 py-4 text-gray-200 hover:text-white transition-colors text-sm tracking-[0.25em] uppercase">
            Buy a license
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="mb-10">
        <video src="/video/sgd-digest.mp4"
               poster="/img/sgd-digest-poster.jpg"
               autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"
               aria-label="A silent screen recording of SGD: drawing a gesture's path on the room floor, shaping its elevation curve, and watching the gestures fly through the room from outside."
               class="w-full border border-gray-800"></video>
        <figcaption class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">
          Edit view — the whole instrument on one screen: gestures on the left, the room floor in the middle,
          the curve editor below it, and the keyboard they all play from along the bottom. Drawing a path,
          shaping its curves, sizing the room, then out to the observe view.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        SGD turns a sound file into a <em class="not-italic text-white">gesture</em>: a sound together with its
        motion through a virtual room around the listener. You draw the path on the room floor, lift it into
        three dimensions with an elevation curve, bend the timing with a motion curve, and bind the result to a
        MIDI key. Pressing that key does not merely play the sound, it sends it traveling — around you,
        overhead, past your ear.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        SGD does not pan. It binauralizes every gesture against a physical model of the room, so on headphones
        the sound leaves your head, with distance, air, wall reflections and Doppler all following from the space
        you built. The whole spatial computation runs offline in the background, so playback itself costs almost
        nothing — and every gesture still keeps its own mixer strip with gain, three-band EQ and a send to the
        shared room reverb.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-16">
        SGD is developed by a former employee of ZKM Karlsruhe and Dear Reality (acquired by Sennheiser), who
        has worked in spatial audio for over a decade.
      </p>

      <!-- ── PITCHES ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-10 gap-y-14 mb-16">

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-gesture.png" alt="The gesture list: each row shows a key dropdown, the gesture name, its sound file and length, and a thumbnail of its path."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">A sound, a path, a key</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            That is a gesture, and the list keeps all three together: the sound file it plays, a thumbnail of the
            path it flies, and the key it answers to. Pick a new key from the dropdown and the binding moves with
            it — up to 128 gestures in a room, each with its own color.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-key.png" alt="The keyboard strip: colored dots on C4, D4, E4 and the black keys mark the gestures bound to each key."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Play space like an instrument</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Every gesture lives on a MIDI key, marked by its own color on the keyboard. Spatial sound design
            stops being an automation-lane chore and becomes something you perform live, from your DAW or the
            standalone application.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-trajectory.png" alt="The trajectory editor: a looping path drawn around the listener with the sample's waveform painted along it."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Draw the motion, sculpt the time</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            The waveform is painted along the trajectory, so you see which part of the sample happens where. The
            motion curve then lets the source rush, hesitate, freeze mid-air, or run the path backwards.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-elevation.png" alt="The elevation editor: breakpoints above and below the listener's ear line define the height of the path."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Lift it off the floor, stretch it wide</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            One editor, three curves. Elevation lifts the path over your head or drops it to your feet; the
            width curve spreads the two channels of a stereo file apart like wingtips, opening from a point into
            a wide wash and closing again.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-render.png" alt="The render panel: Direct plus first, second and third order reflections, a Doppler amount knob, and a background render progress bar."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Sound that leaves your head</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            True binaural rendering, with distance, air absorption and up to three orders of wall reflections.
            Dial the reflections deeper for dense, vivid spaces, and set the Doppler shift of moving sources to
            taste.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-room.png" alt="The room settings dialog: a wireframe room with the listener at its center, size in meters, and wall material controls."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Rooms are real, and they are yours</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Width, height and depth in meters, with a wall material of your choice — absorption, damping,
            scatter and RT60. Resize the room or swap concrete for carpet and the reflections, the reverb and
            every gesture adapt automatically. Rooms save as self-contained folders, samples included.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-mix.png" alt="The per-gesture mix strip: gain, low, mid and high EQ knobs, and a send to the shared room reverb."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Every gesture keeps its own strip</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Gain, three-band EQ and a send to the shared room reverb, per gesture. Nothing is ever rendered
            twice: reopen a room and it is instantly ready; tweak a curve and only that one gesture quietly
            re-renders while you keep working.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div class="border border-gray-800 bg-black h-52 flex items-center justify-center p-3 mb-4">
            <img src="/img/sgd-trim.png" alt="The trim dialog: a stereo waveform with a highlighted region and fade handles at each edge."
                 class="max-h-full max-w-full object-contain" />
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Only the part that flies</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Drag over the waveform to keep the part of the sound you want, pull the triangles for fades, and
            slide the whole region along the file. The gesture and its painted trajectory redraw around whatever
            you keep.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <figure>
        <img src="/img/sgd-observe.png" alt="The SGD observe view: the room as a wireframe box seen from outside, with four named gestures tracing colored paths around the listener."
             class="w-full border border-gray-800" />
        <figcaption class="text-gray-400 text-sm mt-3">
          Observe view — the room from outside at true scale, the listener at its center, every sounding gesture
          named and tracing its path in its own color, each with a glowing sphere that swells and fades with the
          loudness of the sound.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- ── DEMOS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="demos" class="mt-20 border-t border-gray-900 pt-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gray-300 mb-6">Demos</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Five screen recordings, each with the binaural output of SGD itself as its soundtrack. Step through them
        with the arrows — nothing plays until you press play, and only one plays at a time.
      </p>

      <div class="border border-gray-600 px-5 py-4 mb-10 flex items-start gap-4 sm:gap-5">
        <svg class="shrink-0 w-7 h-7 sm:w-8 sm:h-8 text-gray-300 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
             stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
             aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M3 14h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v3a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a9 9 0 0 1 18 0v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-1a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-3a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3"/>
        </svg>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.25em] uppercase text-gray-300 mb-2">
            Put headphones on first
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            These clips are binaural: the whole point is that each ear hears its own signal. Over speakers both
            signals reach both ears, the cues cancel, and the sound just comes from wherever your monitors are —
            there is nothing left to demonstrate. On headphones the same file puts the source out in the room,
            behind you, above you, passing your ear.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-4 border-b border-gray-900 mb-5">
        <div class="flex gap-4 sm:gap-6 overflow-x-auto [scrollbar-width:none] [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden">
          <button type="button" data-demo-tab
                  class="shrink-0 pb-3 -mb-px border-b-2 border-transparent text-[11px] tracking-[0.15em]
                         sm:tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200 transition-colors
                         aria-[current=true]:text-white aria-[current=true]:border-gray-400">Position</button>
          <button type="button" data-demo-tab
                  class="shrink-0 pb-3 -mb-px border-b-2 border-transparent text-[11px] tracking-[0.15em]
                         sm:tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200 transition-colors
                         aria-[current=true]:text-white aria-[current=true]:border-gray-400">Movement</button>
          <button type="button" data-demo-tab
                  class="shrink-0 pb-3 -mb-px border-b-2 border-transparent text-[11px] tracking-[0.15em]
                         sm:tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200 transition-colors
                         aria-[current=true]:text-white aria-[current=true]:border-gray-400">Stereo</button>
          <button type="button" data-demo-tab
                  class="shrink-0 pb-3 -mb-px border-b-2 border-transparent text-[11px] tracking-[0.15em]
                         sm:tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200 transition-colors
                         aria-[current=true]:text-white aria-[current=true]:border-gray-400">Sync</button>
          <button type="button" data-demo-tab
                  class="shrink-0 pb-3 -mb-px border-b-2 border-transparent text-[11px] tracking-[0.15em]
                         sm:tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200 transition-colors
                         aria-[current=true]:text-white aria-[current=true]:border-gray-400">Ideas</button>
        </div>

        <div class="flex shrink-0 gap-1 pb-2">
          <button type="button" data-demo-nav="prev" aria-label="Previous demo"
                  class="w-8 h-8 border border-gray-500 text-gray-300 hover:text-white hover:border-gray-300
                         transition-colors disabled:opacity-25 disabled:hover:text-gray-300
                         disabled:hover:border-gray-500">&#8592;</button>
          <button type="button" data-demo-nav="next" aria-label="Next demo"
                  class="w-8 h-8 border border-gray-500 text-gray-300 hover:text-white hover:border-gray-300
                         transition-colors disabled:opacity-25 disabled:hover:text-gray-300
                         disabled:hover:border-gray-500">&#8594;</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="demo-track"
           class="flex overflow-x-auto snap-x snap-mandatory [scrollbar-width:none]
                  [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden">
          <figure class="w-full shrink-0 snap-start" aria-label="Position">
            <div class="relative">
              <video src="/video/sgd-position.mp4"
                     poster="/img/sgd-position-poster.jpg"
                     data-poster="/img/sgd-position-poster.jpg"
                     controls preload="none" playsinline
                     class="w-full border border-gray-800 bg-black"></video>

              <button type="button" data-demo-play aria-label="Play this demo"
                      class="absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2
                             w-28 h-20 sm:w-36 sm:h-24 rounded-2xl border border-gray-500
                             bg-black/70 text-gray-100 flex items-center justify-center
                             transition duration-200 hover:border-white hover:bg-black/90
                             hover:text-white">
                <svg class="w-12 h-12 sm:w-16 sm:h-16 ml-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"
                     aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4">
              One sound, one point, moved around the room between takes — front, behind, to either side, overhead,
              close and far. Nothing is panned: each position is binauralized against the room, so the source stays
              outside your head and the direction is heard rather than inferred from a level difference.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="w-full shrink-0 snap-start" aria-label="Movement">
            <div class="relative">
              <video src="/video/sgd-movement.mp4"
                     data-poster="/img/sgd-movement-poster.jpg"
                     controls preload="none" playsinline
                     class="w-full border border-gray-800 bg-black"></video>

              <button type="button" data-demo-play aria-label="Play this demo"
                      class="absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2
                             w-28 h-20 sm:w-36 sm:h-24 rounded-2xl border border-gray-500
                             bg-black/70 text-gray-100 flex items-center justify-center
                             transition duration-200 hover:border-white hover:bg-black/90
                             hover:text-white">
                <svg class="w-12 h-12 sm:w-16 sm:h-16 ml-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"
                     aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4">
              The same sound set in motion along a handful of plain paths — straight across from left to right, out
              and back, around a square, down a zigzag — and then the motion curve bent so the source rushes through
              one stretch of the path and lingers over the next.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="w-full shrink-0 snap-start" aria-label="Stereo">
            <div class="relative">
              <video src="/video/sgd-stereo.mp4"
                     data-poster="/img/sgd-stereo-poster.jpg"
                     controls preload="none" playsinline
                     class="w-full border border-gray-800 bg-black"></video>

              <button type="button" data-demo-play aria-label="Play this demo"
                      class="absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2
                             w-28 h-20 sm:w-36 sm:h-24 rounded-2xl border border-gray-500
                             bg-black/70 text-gray-100 flex items-center justify-center
                             transition duration-200 hover:border-white hover:bg-black/90
                             hover:text-white">
                <svg class="w-12 h-12 sm:w-16 sm:h-16 ml-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"
                     aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4">
              A stereo file is placed as two sources rather than one, and the width envelope under the room says
              where each channel sits at every moment. The same marching band is played five ways: the pair stepped
              apart, left and right exchanged, the stage opened gradually from a point to its full width, the pair
              pushed apart by distance, and spread front to back around you.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="w-full shrink-0 snap-start" aria-label="Sync">
            <div class="relative">
              <video src="/video/sgd-sync.mp4"
                     data-poster="/img/sgd-sync-poster.jpg"
                     controls preload="none" playsinline
                     class="w-full border border-gray-800 bg-black"></video>

              <button type="button" data-demo-play aria-label="Play this demo"
                      class="absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2
                             w-28 h-20 sm:w-36 sm:h-24 rounded-2xl border border-gray-500
                             bg-black/70 text-gray-100 flex items-center justify-center
                             transition duration-200 hover:border-white hover:bg-black/90
                             hover:text-white">
                <svg class="w-12 h-12 sm:w-16 sm:h-16 ml-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"
                     aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4">
              The sample's waveform is painted along the trajectory, so every event in the file has a visible place on
              the path. Line a transient up with a corner and the hit lands exactly there — the sound and the space
              it moves through are edited as one thing, by eye.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="w-full shrink-0 snap-start" aria-label="Ideas">
            <div class="relative">
              <video src="/video/sgd-ideas.mp4"
                     data-poster="/img/sgd-ideas-poster.jpg"
                     controls preload="none" playsinline
                     class="w-full border border-gray-800 bg-black"></video>

              <button type="button" data-demo-play aria-label="Play this demo"
                      class="absolute left-1/2 top-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2
                             w-28 h-20 sm:w-36 sm:h-24 rounded-2xl border border-gray-500
                             bg-black/70 text-gray-100 flex items-center justify-center
                             transition duration-200 hover:border-white hover:bg-black/90
                             hover:text-white">
                <svg class="w-12 h-12 sm:w-16 sm:h-16 ml-1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"
                     aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"/>
                </svg>
              </button>
            </div>
            <figcaption class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4">
              A handful of sketches of what the thing is actually for: a siren crossing the room, footsteps circling
              behind you, a whisper arriving at one ear, dogs somewhere off in the dark, a marching band passing by.
              Each one is a sound, a path and a key.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── DOWNLOAD ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section id="download" class="scroll-mt-8 mt-20 border-t border-gray-900 pt-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gray-300 mb-6">Download</h2>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="https://download.radical-process.com/mac/SGD-latest.zip"
           class="block border border-gray-500 hover:border-gray-300 px-6 py-5 text-gray-200 hover:text-white transition-colors">
          <span class="block text-sm tracking-[0.25em] uppercase">Download for macOS</span>
          <span class="block text-gray-400 text-xs mt-2 tracking-wide uppercase">
            Apple Silicon &nbsp;·&nbsp; VST3 / AU / Standalone
          </span>
        </a>

        <div class="border border-gray-800 px-6 py-5 text-gray-400">
          <span class="block text-sm tracking-[0.25em] uppercase">Windows</span>
          <span class="block text-xs mt-2 tracking-wide uppercase">Coming in v1.1 &nbsp;·&nbsp; later in 2026</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-3 mt-4">
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs tracking-wide uppercase">
          14-day free trial &nbsp;·&nbsp; every feature unlocked &nbsp;·&nbsp; no registration
        </p>
        <a href="/manual/sgd/"
           class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white text-xs tracking-[0.25em] uppercase underline underline-offset-4 decoration-gray-500 transition-colors">
          User manual &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── SPECS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="mt-20 border-t border-gray-900 pt-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gray-300 mb-6">Specs</h2>

      <dl class="text-sm border-t border-gray-900 mb-6">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-gray-900 py-3">
          <dt class="w-40 shrink-0 text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs pt-0.5">Platform</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-300">
            macOS 11 (Big Sur) or later, Apple Silicon (ARM) only
            <span class="block text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Windows coming in v1.1, later in 2026</span>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-gray-900 py-3">
          <dt class="w-40 shrink-0 text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs pt-0.5">Formats</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-300">
            VST3, AU, Standalone
            <span class="block text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">AAX (Pro Tools) coming in v2.0</span>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-gray-900 py-3">
          <dt class="w-40 shrink-0 text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs pt-0.5">Sample rates</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-300">44.1, 48 and 96 kHz only</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-1 border-b border-gray-900 py-3">
          <dt class="w-40 shrink-0 text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-xs pt-0.5">Tested hosts</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-300">Logic Pro, Cubase, REAPER</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The macOS build needs macOS 11 (Big Sur) or above and runs on Apple Silicon (ARM) only — there is no
        Intel build, and it will not run on Intel Macs, including under Rosetta. Sessions must run at 44.1, 48
        or 96 kHz; other sample rates are not supported.
      </p>
